---
/**
 * Deploys and packaging. Figures: `src/data/deploy-benchmarks.json`, preliminary run of 22 Oct 2026 (Git push on
 * 23 Oct). Charts go fastest to slowest and include the cases where Stacktape is slower.
 */
import BenchChart from './BenchChart.astro';
import Block from './Block.astro';
---

<Block
  id="deploys"
  marker="Deploys"
  problem="AWS CDK takes 71.8 seconds to get a code change to 25 Lambda functions live."
  title="Stacktape does it in 14.5 seconds."
>
  <p>
    It packages those 25 functions in 3.8 seconds from an empty cache; CDK takes 17.6. A container code change goes live
    in 4.1 to 7.6 seconds with code swap. Code swap covers code changes only: a dependency change uses a normal image
    deploy, which is slower than Heroku.
  </p>
  <p>A pull request rule gives each pull request its own preview stage and can delete it when the pull request closes.</p>
  <p class="deploys__meta">
    Preliminary results, medians in seconds. Measured on 22 Oct 2026, except Stacktape's Git pushes (23 Oct, code swapped
    in place). Heroku's Git push time is its build from the pushed source.
  </p>
  <p class="deploys__meta"><a class="brand-link" href="/benchmarks">How we measured, and every result</a></p>

  <div slot="picture" class="deploys__charts">
    <BenchChart
      comparison="lambda-deploy"
      view="handler"
      app="lambda-25"
      title="Code change to 25 Lambda functions"
      detail="CLI deploy"
    />
    <BenchChart
      comparison="container-deploy"
      view="code-change"
      app="container-node"
      title="Code change to a Node.js container"
      detail="Stacktape with code swap, opt-in"
    />
    <BenchChart comparison="git-push" view="warm" app="container-node" title="Git push, Node.js service" detail="warm runner · Stacktape 23 Oct, others 22 Oct" />
    <BenchChart
      comparison="git-push"
      view="warm"
      app="container-python"
      title="Git push, Python service"
      detail="warm runner · Stacktape 23 Oct, others 22 Oct"
    />
    <BenchChart
      comparison="lambda-deploy"
      view="shared"
      app="lambda-5"
      title="Shared-code change to 5 Lambda functions"
      detail="CLI deploy"
    />
    <BenchChart
      comparison="packaging"
      view="empty-cache"
      app="lambda-25"
      title="Package 25 Lambda functions"
      detail="empty build cache"
    />
  </div>
</Block>

<style>
  .deploys__meta {
    font-size: var(--brand-type-sm);
  }

  .deploys__charts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--brand-space-4);
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .deploys__charts {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
